{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/b1-explainer-about-the-strangest-fruit-combinations-in-real-food-write-like-you-are-talkin/audio/main-338fef36edbe.mp3","durationSec":177.432,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":6.58,"text":"A useful way to understand these foods is to notice three things: the fruit, its partner, and the final result."},{"start":7.8,"end":9.9,"text":"Melon with ham is a clear starting point."},{"start":10.74,"end":15.92,"text":"It is a specialty in Spanish, Italian, and French cooking, usually served in spring and summer."},{"start":16.7,"end":18.92,"text":"The plate contains melon and slices of ham."},{"start":19.6,"end":24.72,"text":"The ham may be serrano ham from Spain, Bayonne ham from France, or another salty ham."},{"start":25.52,"end":31.76,"text":"In prosciutto e melone, the Italian name for this pairing, sweet melon meets salty cured ham."},{"start":32.48,"end":35.6,"text":"The fruit and meat stay separate and easy to recognize."},{"start":36.36,"end":39.86,"text":"The surprising result comes from the strong difference between their flavors."},{"start":41.2,"end":44.52,"text":"Some combinations place fruit inside a rich meat dish."},{"start":44.52,"end":51.72,"text":"Duck à l’orange is a French dish of roast duck with bigarade sauce, a sauce made with bitter Seville oranges."},{"start":51.72,"end":57.2,"text":"Its main ingredients include duck, orange, butter, stock, sugar, and vinegar."},{"start":58,"end":61.62,"text":"The first published recipe appeared in 1813 in The French Cook."},{"start":61.62,"end":66.74,"text":"Fesenjan is a sweet-and-sour Iranian stew from Gilan."},{"start":66.74,"end":69.68,"text":"It is a khoresh, an Iranian stew served over rice."},{"start":70.5,"end":75.72,"text":"Its main mix is pomegranate juice or paste, ground walnuts, and poultry such as duck or chicken."},{"start":76.34,"end":77.68,"text":"It can also contain other meats."},{"start":78.36,"end":83.28,"text":"Unlike melon with ham, the fruit becomes part of the sauce and gives flavor to the whole dish."},{"start":84.28,"end":87.44,"text":"Green papaya salad shows that a fruit dish does not need to be sweet."},{"start":88.02,"end":90.78,"text":"It is a spicy salad made from shredded unripe papaya."},{"start":91.6,"end":97.12,"text":"In Thailand it is called som tam, the Thai name for this sour, salty, and spicy salad."},{"start":97.74,"end":103.18,"text":"The mix includes sour lime, hot chili, salty fish sauce, and a little palm sugar."},{"start":104.12,"end":105.66,"text":"Dried shrimp may also be included."},{"start":105.66,"end":108.56,"text":"Chamoy offers another surprising use of fruit."},{"start":109.22,"end":112.64,"text":"Chamoy is a Mexican sauce made from pickled fruit, salt, and chili."},{"start":113.18,"end":117.76,"text":"Fruit is packed in brine, which is salty water used for pickling, sometimes with vinegar."},{"start":118.4,"end":120.88,"text":"The fruit brine is then seasoned with chili powder."},{"start":121.38,"end":127.46,"text":"The finished sauce can be put on fresh fruit, adding salty, sour, sweet, and spicy flavors."},{"start":128.62,"end":135.6,"text":"Hawaiian pizza is a Canadian pizza with pineapple, tomato sauce, mozzarella cheese, and ham or bacon."},{"start":136.4,"end":141.78,"text":"Sam Panopoulos is credited with making the first one at the Satellite Restaurant in Ontario in 1962."},{"start":142.8,"end":147.78,"text":"He tried the mix because Canadian Chinese dishes often combine sweet and sour flavors."},{"start":148.44,"end":153.16,"text":"The name came from the canned pineapple brand he used, not from the state of Hawaii."},{"start":153.16,"end":161.24,"text":"Romeu e Julieta is a traditional Brazilian pairing of cheese and goiabada, a thick guava conserve."},{"start":161.55,"end":164.92,"text":"The simplest plate is guava conserve on a slice of cheese."},{"start":165.72,"end":169.38,"text":"It is believed to have begun in Minas Gerais during the colonial period."},{"start":170.02,"end":176.96,"text":"Both dishes place sweet fruit beside salty cheese, but one is a pizza and the other is a simple fruit-and-cheese plate."}],"words":[{"text":"A","start":0,"end":0.14},{"text":"useful","start":0.14,"end":0.44},{"text":"way","start":0.44,"end":0.66},{"text":"to","start":0.66,"end":0.82},{"text":"understand","start":0.82,"end":1.2},{"text":"these","start":1.2,"end":1.44},{"text":"foods","start":1.44,"end":1.78},{"text":"is","start":1.78,"end":2.06},{"text":"to","start":2.06,"end":2.24},{"text":"notice","start":2.24,"end":2.52},{"text":"three","start":2.52,"end":2.86},{"text":"things","start":2.86,"end":3.37},{"text":"the","start":3.37,"end":3.88},{"text":"fruit","start":3.88,"end":4.22},{"text":"its","start":4.7,"end":4.9},{"text":"partner","start":4.9,"end":5.3},{"text":"and","start":5.66,"end":5.82},{"text":"the","start":5.82,"end":5.94},{"text":"final","start":5.94,"end":6.2},{"text":"result","start":6.2,"end":6.58},{"text":"Melon","start":7.8,"end":8},{"text":"with","start":8,"end":8.2},{"text":"ham","start":8.2,"end":8.44},{"text":"is","start":8.44,"end":8.76},{"text":"a","start":8.76,"end":8.9},{"text":"clear","start":8.9,"end":9.16},{"text":"starting","start":9.16,"end":9.56},{"text":"point","start":9.56,"end":9.9},{"text":"It","start":10.74,"end":10.84},{"text":"is","start":10.84,"end":10.94},{"text":"a","start":10.94,"end":11.1},{"text":"specialty","start":11.1,"end":11.38},{"text":"in","start":11.38,"end":11.68},{"text":"Spanish","start":11.68,"end":12.12},{"text":"Italian","start":12.42,"end":12.8},{"text":"and","start":12.82,"end":13},{"text":"French","start":13,"end":13.22},{"text":"cooking","start":13.22,"end":13.62},{"text":"usually","start":14.26,"end":14.48},{"text":"served","start":14.48,"end":14.96},{"text":"in","start":14.96,"end":15.16},{"text":"spring","start":15.16,"end":15.44},{"text":"and","start":15.44,"end":15.62},{"text":"summer","start":15.62,"end":15.92},{"text":"The","start":16.7,"end